## What `:dt/memorial-policy` is

A `:db.type/keyword` slot on `:dt/Class` instances declaring how members of the class are made durable + presented across the substrate / corpus boundary.  Introduced 2026-05-23 per the SPEC-vs-STATE pivot ratifying [decisions/option_b_plus_c_ratified_spec_vs_state_criterion_pivot_to_first_class_memorialization_2026_05_23.md](../decisions/option_b_plus_c_ratified_spec_vs_state_criterion_pivot_to_first_class_memorialization_2026_05_23.md).

The slot composes with `:dt/native-codec` (codec format selection) + `:dt/codec-aliases` (per-class slot-name aliasing) + `:dt/codec-slot-order` (canonical frontmatter emit order) + `:dt/bm25f-weights` (per-class fulltext weights) to form the per-class projection-control surface.

## The three values

| Value | Semantics | Example classes |
|---|---|---|
| `:first-class` | Instances project to `memory/<class-path>/<ident>.md` via `sandbar.reactive.sinks/fs-projection-sink`.  BM25F-searchable.  Human-editable.  Git-versioned alongside corpus memorials. | `:mm/Memory` (and descendants by hierarchy walk), `:workflow/Definition`, future `:scheduler/Schedule` + `:scheduler/Job` |
| `:db-only` | Instances stay DB-resident.  No fs counterpart.  Covered by the DB-dump arc (phantom-ref/branch in git) for disaster recovery + audit.  Not searchable via BM25F (no body content). | `:workflow/Process`, future `:scheduler/Process`, `:dt/Class`, `:dt/Property`, `:event/HttpRequest` |
| `:inline` | Instances serialize inline within host memorials' slot values.  No standalone fs file (cardinality would explode the fs tree).  Searchable indirectly via host memorial's body / slots. | `:mm/Tag` (serialized in `:mm.memory/tags` slot of host memorials) |

## Why this exists

Pre-pivot, the substrate had several classes (`:workflow/Definition` etc.) that lived ONLY in the DB — not in the fs corpus.  This broke metacircularity / reflectivity / introspection: the AI couldn't search workflows via BM25F (no body content); couldn't navigate to a workflow's .md file (none existed); couldn't edit workflows via the same authoring path used for decisions / observations.

Post-pivot, `:dt/memorial-policy` makes the classification DECLARATIVE + INTROSPECTABLE.  The substrate's reactive-projection sink consults it at projection time; the DB-dump worker consults it at dump time.  Future class authoring is required to declare the policy explicitly (per [plans/sandbar_first_class_memorialization_arc_workflows_schedules_contexts_dt_memorial_policy_2026_05_23.md](../plans/sandbar_first_class_memorialization_arc_workflows_schedules_contexts_dt_memorial_policy_2026_05_23.md) §6.7 Stage G).

## Inheritance semantics

`:dt/memorial-policy` is declared per-class.  Subclasses inherit via `:dt/subclass-of` walk if not overridden — implemented in the consumer (fs-projection-sink walks the class hierarchy looking for the closest declaration).  `:mm/Memory` declares `:first-class` once; all 40+ descendants inherit.  Specific classes override (`:event/HttpRequest` declares `:db-only` even though it descends from `:mm/Memory`).

## Substrate-side enforcement

- **`sandbar.reactive.sinks/fs-projection-sink`** (Stage B.3 of the first-class-memorialization arc): consults `:dt/memorial-policy` before invoking codec.emit + fs.write.  Skips classes with `:db-only` or `:inline` policy.
- **`sandbar.project.dump-db-only`** (Stage B of the DB-dump arc): walks classes; includes only those with `:db-only` policy.
- **Class registration validation** (future; Stage G of the first-class-memorialization arc): loud-fails on `:dt/Class` instances without explicit `:dt/memorial-policy` declaration.

